---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { storyPages, storyPath } from '../../lib/story';
---

<Layout
  title="The story — The nnxyz Rooms"
  description="The drawing board, the collector, his fan art, the artist's project, the year 2022 and the artist's own words: the story behind the rooms, from the archive, the ledger and the record."
>
  <article class="text-page story-index">
    <h1>The story</h1>
    <p>
      The rooms show the art. These pages tell what was around it: the drawing
      board that kept every stroke, the collector who kept buying, the fan art
      he drew one evening, the three years of the artist's project, the year
      most of it was drawn, and what the artist has said in public. Every fact
      on them comes from the archive, the public ledgers, the artist's posts or
      the collector's own published writing, and each page lists its sources.
    </p>
    <ol class="story-list">
      {storyPages.map((page) => (
        <li>
          <a href={storyPath(page.slug)}>{page.title}</a>
          <p>{page.summary}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p>
      A seventh page, <a href="/technique/">Technique</a>, reads the stroke
      record itself: what the order of every mark in 548 drawings shows, and
      twelve works drawn at five points in their build.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/#collections">Enter the collections →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
